# .gitignore — rust-yaml
#
# Kept deliberately lean: only patterns that apply to this Rust crate. Personal
# agent/editor tooling (.idea, .claude, docs/superpowers) is also covered by the
# user's global excludesfile; the IDE + OS entries below are duplicated here so
# the repo stays clean for every contributor and on CI (macOS / Linux / Windows).
#
# cargo-fuzz artifacts (target, corpus, artifacts, coverage) are ignored by
# fuzz/.gitignore, not here.

# ── Rust / Cargo ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.orig

# Cargo.lock IS committed: it pins the dependency graph for reproducible builds
# across the stable/beta/nightly × {ubuntu,macos,windows} CI matrix.

# ── Coverage & profiling ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
lcov.info
*.profraw
*.profdata

# Flamegraph / perf artifacts — see docs/PROFILING.md
flamegraph*.svg
*.flamegraph.svg
perf.data
perf.data.old
cargo-flamegraph.trace/
*.stacks
*.dtrace.stacks
*.folded

# ── Project scratch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/RELEASE_NOTES.md
/debug_*
/test_*
debug_*
test_*

# ── Editors & IDEs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── OS files ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# macOS
.DS_Store
._*
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Linux
.directory
.nfs*
.Trash-*

# Windows
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# ── Agent tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Also covered by most contributors' global excludesfile, but declared here on
# purpose: tools that walk the tree themselves do NOT read the global one.
# `.claude/worktrees/<branch>/` is a checked-out git worktree carrying its own
# 1.4 GB target/ directory, and scanning it made gitleaks report mangled Rust
# symbols in compiled .o files as `generic-api-key` findings that blocked a
# commit. taplo needed the same exclusion for the same reason (see taplo.toml).
.claude/

# ── mise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Machine-specific, regenerated by `mise run setup`. mise.toml and mise.lock ARE
# committed; this file only ever records which tools Homebrew already satisfies.
mise.local.toml

# ── Misc ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.bak
*.tmp
.env
.env.local
/cobertura.xml

# ── NodeJS / Vitepress / TypeScript ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/**/node_modules/
/**/dist/

# Playwright MCP scratch output (snapshots, console logs, screenshots). Written
# to the repo root by default, so it needs ignoring or it lands in a commit.
/**/.playwright-mcp/

# `cache/deps/` alone left the rest of .vitepress/cache/ trackable — VitePress
# writes more than the dependency cache there, so ignore the whole directory.
/**/.vitepress/cache/
/**/cache/deps/
/**/*.tsbuildinfo
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
